1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,032
Rosetta DBT Studio just leveled up.

2
00:00:03,252 --> 00:00:07,220
Four releases in three weeks, packed with features for analytics engineers.

3
00:00:07,439 --> 00:00:09,040
Here’s what’s new, in two minutes.

4
00:00:10,239 --> 00:00:11,733
It starts with a brand-new home.

5
00:00:11,953 --> 00:00:24,326
The Workspace Overview puts every module one click away: dbt projects, notebooks, the SQL editor, analytics, data lake, pipelines and ETL, right next to your recent projects and connections.

6
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:26,849
Meet Python notebooks.

7
00:00:27,069 --> 00:00:33,768
Query your database in a SQL cell, save the result as a DataFrame, and keep going in pandas in the very next cell.

8
00:00:33,988 --> 00:00:38,126
Every result becomes an interactive table you can filter and page through.

9
00:00:38,346 --> 00:00:41,162
SQL, Python and notes, together in one notebook.

10
00:00:42,362 --> 00:00:43,599
Working with Snowflake?

11
00:00:43,819 --> 00:00:45,654
Now you can sign in through your browser.

12
00:00:45,874 --> 00:00:53,021
Pick Web Browser, test the connection, finish the login on Snowflake’s page, and you’re in, without typing a password into Studio.

13
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,799
MySQL joins the lineup.

14
00:00:56,019 --> 00:01:02,611
Connect in seconds with optional SSL, browse your tables in the schema tree, and run queries in the SQL editor.

15
00:01:02,831 --> 00:01:06,821
New compatibility indicators show which connections work with dbt.

16
00:01:08,021 --> 00:01:09,621
The schema tree got smarter too.

17
00:01:09,841 --> 00:01:16,219
Right-click any table to generate SELECT, COUNT or INSERT statements, copy column lists, or preview the data.

18
00:01:16,439 --> 00:01:18,274
Or just drag it straight into your editor.

19
00:01:18,494 --> 00:01:20,841
It works in both the SQL editor and notebooks.

20
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:23,641
And the AI agent can now see.

21
00:01:23,861 --> 00:01:32,458
Attach a screenshot, a diagram or an error dialog, and the agent reasons over the image together with your project, your files and the conversation.

22
00:01:32,678 --> 00:01:34,705
Just pick a model that supports images.

23
00:01:35,905 --> 00:01:38,486
Plus, a new dbt adapter for Kinetica.

24
00:01:38,706 --> 00:01:42,845
Install it, and update it from source, right from the dbt Core settings.

25
00:01:44,045 --> 00:01:48,781
Rosetta DBT Studio is free, open source, and runs right on your desktop.

26
00:01:49,001 --> 00:01:55,059
Download it at rosettadb.io, give us a star on GitHub, and tell us what you want to see next!
